                <pb facs="0869" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/81: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >George</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-18T10:00:00+02:35">December 18, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. My telegram No. 25.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d655-f1"/> Revolt among Ethiopian
                    desert Somalia rumored. Owing to poor communications secrecy it is impossible to
                    verify rumored internal disorders. I am informed Emperor is considering asking
                    American mediation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
